          "Fingerprint": "sha256:dd1172a74388b26fe25463019fac7f5d4eab38418ad0a9853ef12c672cbaa2f0",
          "Title": "com.google.guava/guava: Google Guava: Denial of Service via unthrottled memory allocation during deserialization",
          "Description": "Allocation of resources without limits or throttling (CWE-770) during Java object deserialization in Google Guava versions 4.0 through 33.7.1 allows an attacker to cause a Denial of Service via OutOfMemoryError. When deserializing CompactHashMap, CompactHashSet, or MapMakerInternalMap instances, Guava eagerly allocates an array based on a caller-specified size parameter without throttling, permitting memory exhaustion from crafted serialization streams.",
